WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
15 January 2015.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.050
Switzerland's central bank
makes one announcement.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.890
Since 2011 it has held a floor:

4
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:12.670
at least 1.20 francs for every euro.

5
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.570
Now it drops that floor,

6
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:19.030
and cuts its interest rate
to minus 0.75 per cent.

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.020
The franc rises sharply against the euro.

8
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.190
Money moves in seconds.

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.730
So how can one decision by a central bank

10
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.920
change what a currency is
worth around the world?

11
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.250
In this mission, you'll meet everyone
who buys and sells a currency.

12
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.220
Then you'll change an interest
rate yourself and watch

13
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.350
the currency market respond.

14
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out why
one decision by a central

15
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.030
bank can change what a currency
is worth around the world.
